                "entry_id": "9addf84b-7816-3814-8c37-52da695a1fd8",
                "word": "Georgie",
                "pos": "name",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "588ece07-efcf-3066-a4b5-a6eee5c92e9f",
                        "entry_id": "9addf84b-7816-3814-8c37-52da695a1fd8",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Georgia (a medieval country in the South Caucasus, approximately coextensive with modern Georgia)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f64dcda8-9679-46f4-9078-a45706f2c0cd",
                                "sense_id": "588ece07-efcf-3066-a4b5-a6eee5c92e9f",
                                "text": "THe realme of Georgie toward thorient hath agret mountayn / which is named Abbers & is inhabited with many diuers nations of peple. And for that cause it is named the countrey Alayne.",
                                "translation": "A lytell cronycle",
                                "english": "A lytell cronycle"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c42d3094-9620-498e-8ba4-86984d10f38b",
                                "sense_id": "588ece07-efcf-3066-a4b5-a6eee5c92e9f",
                                "text": "And after he addreſſed an armie againſt the Soldan of Egipt & the Sarazins of the which his purpose Caſſan aduertiſed the kings of Armenia & Georgie, who with their armies came & ioyned with him at Baudras, and from thence marched to the towne of Hames."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cfbb85a3-2f79-4428-a979-4a6101a5a5c2",
                                "sense_id": "588ece07-efcf-3066-a4b5-a6eee5c92e9f",
                                "text": "In that Citie (of Vaxnan) Frier Bernard Cathalane, of the Order of the Preaching Friers found me; who abode in Georgie, with a certaine Prior of the Sepulcher, who poſſeſſeth great lands there. And he had learned ſomewhat of the Tartars language."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            }
